{
  "slug": "short-asabiyya",
  "id": "short-asabiyya",
  "title": "The curve every empire follows",
  "note": "Ibn Khaldun charted how group solidarity carries a dynasty to power and then lets it fall.",
  "short": true,
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "the-short",
      "title": "The curve every empire follows",
      "theme": "nutvoid",
      "short": true,
      "beats": [
        {
          "kind": "plate",
          "plate": "a-curve-showing-a-group-with-strong-so",
          "hold": 49.2,
          "lines": [
            {
              "text": "Why every empire falls the same way",
              "sub": "a pattern found 650 years ago",
              "size": "hook",
              "at": 0.0,
              "until": 5.84
            },
            {
              "text": "In Algeria, the year 1377",
              "sub": "Ibn Khaldun, a historian, writes a book",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 6.18,
              "until": 11.97
            },
            {
              "text": "A united people rises and takes power",
              "sub": "their strength: they stick together",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 12.31,
              "until": 18.64
            },
            {
              "text": "In power, life gets comfortable",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 18.98,
              "until": 22.16
            },
            {
              "text": "Generation after generation, it fades",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 22.5,
              "until": 26.08
            },
            {
              "text": "A hungrier, united people takes over",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 26.42,
              "until": 29.98
            },
            {
              "text": "Before him, history was just stories",
              "sub": "he made it a science with laws",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 30.32,
              "until": 36.3
            },
            {
              "text": "Nations still rise and fall his way",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 36.64,
              "until": 40.18
            },
            {
              "eyebrow": "Ibn Khaldun, Tunis to Cairo",
              "text": "He called that unity asabiyya",
              "sub": "group feeling, the bond that holds people",
              "src": "The Muqaddimah, 1377",
              "size": "h1",
              "at": 40.52,
              "until": 48.83
            }
